      "sidereal.title": "Fixed Sidereal Time and automatic animation",
      "sidereal.what.title": "What Fixed Sidereal Time does",
      "sidereal.what.body1": "Turn on Fixed Sidereal Time in Local Date and Time when you want to compare the motion of the Sun, Moon, and planets against a stable stellar background.",
      "sidereal.what.body2": "It is available with Minutes, Hours, Day, and Month. With Minutes and Hours, the displayed stellar sky stays fixed while real elapsed time advances. With Day and Month, Time Travel Sky adjusts the civil clock to preserve the same local apparent sidereal time. Year, Century, and Millennium remain normal.",
      "sidereal.controls.title": "How to use the controls",
      "sidereal.controls.checkbox": "In Local Date and Time, check Fixed Sidereal Time, then Apply. Uncheck it to return to normal civil-time stepping.",
